<title>NORWAY: POLL-DnB H1 pre-tax profits seen higher.</title>
<headline>POLL-DnB H1 pre-tax profits seen higher.</headline>
<dateline>OSLO 1997-07-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Den norske Bank (DnB), Norway's biggest bank, is expected to post a first-half 1997 pre-tax operating profit of about 1.55 billion crowns, according to six analysts polled by Reuters.</p>
<p>The corresponding figure for the first half of 1996 was 1.53 billion crowns.</p>
<p>Four analysts had a buy recommendation on the share, one said hold and another said sell.</p>
<p>DnB will present the figures on August 6.</p>
<p>				(millions of crowns unless stated)</p>
<p>				  H1 1997    low    high  H1 1996</p>
<p> Net interest income	 2,127    2,099  2,169   2,115</p>
<p> Other operating income    1,626    1,580  1,686   1,479</p>
<p> Operating expenses	  2,240    2,217  2,257   2,299</p>
<p>Pre-tax operating</p>
<p> profit before losses	1,498    1,433  1,563   1,296</p>
<p> Pre-tax operating profit  1,548    1,476  1,605   1,525</p>
<p> Profit for the period     1,447    1,152  1,593   1,513</p>
<p> EPS (crowns)		  2.26     1.80   2.47    2.36</p>
<p> EPS 1997			3.76     3.20   4.40</p>
<p> EPS 1998			3.16     2.70   3.62</p>
<p> Dividend 1997		 1.61     1.50   1.90</p>
<p>NOTE - One brokerage used a different method for estimating the tax and put it higher than the others. Excluding the estimate of that brokerage, the projected profit for the period based on the other five estimates is 1.51 billion crowns.</p>
<p>--Oslo newsroom, Alf Asklund +47 22 93 69 71</p>
